## 00. QA Workflow — Driving a Ticket

The AI agent (you) drives tickets through the QA pipeline by reconstructing current state
from live artifacts, then spawning the correct sub-agent for the missing phase. There is
no stored state machine — **the live artifacts are the state.**

### Invocation

The user hands over a ticket key (`{{ tracker_project_key }}-NNNN`{% if tracker == 'github_issues' %} or issue number{% endif %}).
That key is the universal join key embedded in every artifact (TD doc title, test case
Refs field, run name) and is how you find prior work.

### Cold-start reconstruction — do this first, every time

1. **Read `.claude/references/` first** — the living cache records what has already been
   created (test sections, automation coverage, project constants).
2. **On a cache miss, query the live systems** ({{ doc_label }}, {{ test_repo_label }},
   {{ tracker_label }}) using the ticket key as the search anchor.
3. **If nothing exists for the ticket, spawn sub-agents** to create it (test-design → bdd).

{{ comm_platform_label if has_comm_platform else "Slack" }} is **notify-only** — never
use it as a reconstruction source.

### Phase-derivation table

| Probe | Finding | Next action |
|---|---|---|
| {{ tracker_label }} ticket | Missing or no Acceptance Criteria | Halt → escalate to human{% if has_comm_platform %} via {{ comm_platform_label }}{% endif %} |
| {{ doc_label }} TD doc (key in title) | None found | Spawn **test-design-agent** |
| TD doc | Status = *In Review* | Spawn **bdd-agent** |
| TD doc | Status = *Approved* | Continue to test repo probe |
{% if has_test_repo %}
| {{ test_repo_label }} (Refs = key) | Approved TD but no cases | Spawn **bdd-agent** |
| {{ test_repo_label }} | Cases exist, no run / results | Spawn **manual-agent** |
| {{ test_repo_label }} run | All cases have results | Continue to automation probe |
| `automation-coverage.md` / spec tags | ≥1 automatable case with no spec tag | Spawn **automation-agent** |
| `automation-coverage.md` / spec tags | No pending rows (all automated or excluded) | **Done** → final compliance score{% if has_comm_platform %} + advisory to {{ comm_platform_label }}{% endif %} |
{% endif %}

### Dispatch + handoff rules

- Spawn sub-agents **serially, one at a time** — never two concurrently for the same ticket.
- Every dispatch passes the **handoff contract** (`.claude/skills/handoff-protocol.md`):
  required keys + `actions_taken` + `routing` + `writeback_targets`.
- After a sub-agent creates a remote artifact, perform the **`.md` write-back**: update
  `.claude/references/test-sections.md` (new section) or `automation-coverage.md`
  (new automation rows) so the next cold-start session does not need a live query.

### Inline compliance gate

After **each** sub-agent returns, run `convention-check` on its output:

- `critical > 0` → re-dispatch that same phase with the findings attached.
- **After 3 rewrites of the same phase** → escalate to human{% if has_comm_platform %} via
  {{ comm_platform_label }}{% endif %} and halt.
- On manual verdicts: `failed_requirement` → route rework to test-design-agent;
  `failed_scenario` → app bug (use `report-bug` skill). Each counts against the rewrite ceiling.

### Reference directives

| Situation | Read first |
